    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d651">

                <pb facs="1312" n="1290" xml:id="pg1290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.A.L./2–1246: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic Officers
                        </hi><anchor n="38" xml:id="d651-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-02-12T18:00:00-05:00">February 12,
                            1946—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dept will transmit to you, within next few days, third person air mail
                    instruction enclosing copies of a memorandum dated Feb 6 entitled “Preparations
                    for Preliminary Meeting on Trade and Employment”.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d651-f2"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Please transmit copies of this memorandum to appropriate officials of Govt to
                    which you are accredited, stating that it represents the ideas of the Govt of
                    the US regarding <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) the objectives of the meeting,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the procedures which appear to be desirable
                    before and at the meeting to achieve these objectives and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>) the relation between the preliminary meeting and
                    the proposed general world conference on trade and employment. You may also add
                    that Govt of US would be glad to receive views of Govt to which you are
                    accredited regarding any of suggestions put forward in memorandum.<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d651-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Copies will also be made available informally to missions of nuclear countries in
                    Washington.</p>
                <p>In connection with foregoing, US delegation to UNO has intoduced resolution in
                    Economic and Social Council for calling of world conference on trade and
                    employment which will be discussed by Council in next day or two. Text of
                    resolution follows in subsequent circular telegram.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d651-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d651-f1" n="38" type="source" xml:id="d651-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the fifteen United States missions accredited to the governments invited
                    by the United States to the preliminary conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d651-f2" n="39" xml:id="d651-f2-content">
                <p>The memorandum was transmitted under cover of instructions dated February 15,
                    none printed. On the same date, February 15, the Department sent a circular
                    telegram to the same missions instructing them to withhold conveyance of the
                    memorandum to the government concerned until informed by the Department that
                    ECOSOC had acted on the proposed resolution on the trade and employment
                    conference (560.AL/2–1546).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d651-f3" n="40" xml:id="d651-f3-content">
                <p>The Department authorized transmission of the memorandum to the appropriate
                    governments in a circular telegram of February 20, 7 p.m. (560.AL/2–1546).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d651-f4" n="41" xml:id="d651-f4-content">
                <p>The draft of this resolution is printed in telegram 797, January 22, <ref
                        target="#pg1277">p. 1277</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
